=== AC1 — EXPLAIN on representative storage() eager-load, PRE vs POST migration ===

Real ORM query captured via `php artisan tinker` (Item::with('storage')->limit(20)->get()):
  select * from `storages` where `storages`.`data_id` in (1,2,...,20)
    and `storages`.`data_type` = 'App\Models\Item'

PRE-migration (EXPLAIN FORMAT=TRADITIONAL):
  id | select_type | table    | type | possible_keys          | key  | rows | Extra
   1 | SIMPLE      | storages | ALL  | storages_data_id_index | NULL | 1309 | Using where
  -> full table scan (varchar data_id vs int literals defeats the single-col index)

POST-migration (same query, EXPLAIN FORMAT=TRADITIONAL):
  id | select_type | table    | type  | possible_keys                    | key                               | rows | Extra
   1 | SIMPLE      | storages | range | storages_data_type_data_id_index | storages_data_type_data_id_index  |  78  | Using index condition
  -> index range scan via the new composite (data_type, data_id) index, 1309 -> 78 rows examined

VERDICT: PASS — type=ALL/table scan (pre) -> type=range/index lookup (post), confirmed independently.

=== AC2 — row count unchanged, no data loss/corruption ===

PRE-migration:  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM storages;              => 1309
POST-migration: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM storages;               => 1309
POST-rollback:  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM storages;               => 1309

Schema PRE:  data_id varchar(100), index storages_data_id_index (data_id)
Schema POST: data_id bigint unsigned, index storages_data_type_data_id_index (data_type, data_id)
Schema POST-ROLLBACK: data_id varchar(100), index storages_data_id_index (data_id)  [== PRE, exact]

Spot-check data integrity (per-data_type COUNT + SUM(data_id) post-migration, cross-checked
against sampled pre-migration rows): Item type had 866 rows summing to 490359; sampled rows
(id=50/51 -> data_id=1, id=213/214 -> data_id=2, id=215 -> data_id=3) match the pre-migration
values exactly — cast BIGINT UNSIGNED preserved every value bit-for-bit (all storages.data_id
values were purely numeric, confirmed by the migration's own pre-flight REGEXP guard which found
0 non-numeric rows and did not abort).

VERDICT: PASS — 1309 -> 1309 -> 1309, zero data loss/corruption, migration is cleanly reversible.

=== AC3 — no visual/data regression on screens reading images via storage() ===

Path taken: booted the real Admin backend (php artisan serve --port=8091) against the
POST-migration isolated clone DB (multi_food_db_test_nears_nears_2987_storages_data_id_index,
NEVER the shared multi_food_db, NEVER the shared port-8000 instance), then drove the real public
API endpoints UserApp/StoreApp actually call, which resolve images via storage()/get_full_url():

GET /api/v1/stores/details/1 (zoneId header only, unauthenticated, public endpoint)
  -> "storage": [{"data_type":"App\\Models\\Store","data_id":1,"key":"logo",...},
                 {"data_type":"App\\Models\\Store","data_id":1,"key":"cover_photo",...}]
     (exactly the 2 rows for this store, correctly joined post-migration BIGINT data_id=1)
  -> "logo_full_url": ".../storage/store/2024-11-19-673c404ae469c.png"
  -> "cover_photo_full_url": ".../storage/store/cover/2024-11-19-673c404ae633e.png"

GET /api/v1/items/details/1 (zoneId + moduleId headers, unauthenticated, public endpoint)
  -> item "storage" (2 rows: image, images), nested store_details.storage (2 rows),
     nested category_details[].storage (per-category rows), nested module.storage (5 rows)
     — every morph relation resolved the CORRECT rows for its own data_id post-migration.
  -> image_full_url / images_full_url / category image_full_url / module icon+thumbnail
     full_url all populated correctly.

Image bytes fetched directly from the running server (proves the storage()-resolved paths are
real, not just present in JSON):
  GET /storage/store/2024-11-19-673c404ae469c.png        -> 200 image/png 3120B   (store logo)
  GET /storage/store/cover/2024-11-19-673c404ae633e.png  -> 200 image/png 7880B   (store cover)
  GET /storage/product/2024-11-19-673c408cf104a.png      -> 200 image/png 61555B  (item image)
  GET /storage/product/2024-11-19-673c408cedb59.png      -> 200 image/png 9523B   (item gallery image)
  GET /storage/category/2024-11-19-673c3ffb0a6f7.png     -> 200 image/png 13772B  (category image)
  GET /storage/module/2026-03-01-9f4876593842.png        -> 200 image/png 34393B  (module thumbnail)

All 6 images across Store/Item/Category/Module (all use the same storage() morphMany relation as
User/Banner) resolved with HTTP 200 + correct image/png content-type + non-zero byte sizes,
served by a live backend running against the POST-migration schema. No broken images, no 404s,
